PHASE 3 — pipeline capture by APPENDING a stage (§0c). Never prepend to a pipeline.
Rewrite form:
  <orig> | <bin> filter [--hint <preset>] --ref <nonce>; <bin> status "${pipestatus[k]:-${PIPESTATUS[k-1]:-$?}}"
  - <orig> is the original command text, byte-for-byte untouched. Only constant text is added.
  - <bin> = `ldm-compress` if shutil.which("ldm-compress") realpaths to the plugin binary,
    else the absolute path.
  - k = number of stages in the LAST pipeline (zsh is 1-based; bash index is one less;
    $? covers the case where an earlier `cd` failed and the pipeline never ran).
  - nonce = 8 hex chars. The hook writes ~/.cache/ldm-compress/pending/<nonce>.json
    {cmd, shape, session, hint, ts} so the original command reaches the outputs row without
    ever being passed as a shell argument.

New subcommands:
  filter [--hint P] [--ref N] [--max-bytes B]: read all of stdin as bytes. If len ≤
    default_max_bytes (4096, per-repo override, --max-bytes) → write stdin to stdout
    byte-identical, no footer, no store. Else → store as an outputs row (source='filter',
    cmd/shape from the pending file, consume it), index, render with the same renderer as
    `run`: preset if --hint given and its json_path matches, otherwise generic slicing
    (never the "structure only" empty-match view for pipelines). Footer format identical
    to run's, omitting the exit field, using <bin>. Empty stdin → print nothing.
  status <N>: sys.exit(int(N)); non-integer/empty → exit 0 and log a warning.

